{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/39604-actual-play-dead-men-and-sinners","id":39604,"title":"[Actual Play] Dead Men and Sinners","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-30T14:42:15-08:00","id":39604,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [Actual Play] Dead Men and Sinners","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I did a one-shot of Geist during the Golden Age of Piracy, and it was tons of fun. Sadly I wasn't able to do everything I wanted, but we will probably play this again when we get together again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here's the actual play!</span></span> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><img src=\"http://pedro.coppola.bz/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/pirate1.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Nicholas &quot;Old Nicky&quot; Groot</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Archetype: Celebrant</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Threshold: The Torn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Geist: Lazarus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Keystone: Shovel</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nicholas was an artist and a painter, enamorated with life. Till he tried to seduce the daughter of a bureaucrat and was hunted by the bureaucrat's henchmen and thwacked in the head to the brink of death. His Geist is Lazarus, an old man who had to dig his own grave before dying. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Bernard</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Archetype: Reaper</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Threshold: The Prey</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Geist: The Jester</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Keystone: Ivory Teeth</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bernard travels a lot. He usually finds work in the taverns, stays for a few months and leave. A natural and passionated Hunter, till one day he was almost mauled to death by a black jaguar. His body is covered by scars to remind him of that day. His Geist was a Jester that had his head smashed by an elephant. The Jester now has the head of an Elephant while wearing makeup. Very creepy. :P</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Andrew Milles</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Archetype: Bonepicker</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Threshold: The Stricken</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Geist: The Dark Monk</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Keystone: Crucifix</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Andrew was a member of the British Navy, till he was stricken with sickness and left to die in an island in the middle of nowhere. There, he bounded with the Dark Monk, a plague-afflicted monk with hundreds of flies following around. The Dark Monk helped him shape his body in a better way that he was able to swim back to civilization.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Javier Hernandez</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Archetype: Bonepicker</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Threshold: The Forgotten</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Geist: Hisham</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Keystone: Jeweled Necklace</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Javier was a master cannoneer and a member of the spanish fleet, till the English attacked his ship and destroyed it. He was actually killed by a falling mast. His Geist was a weaponsmith for a calipha. Till a cannonball shook the tower he was working in, spilling molten metal in his body. Then he dropped from the window. Very nasty looking. Javier also has a hammer that is a deathmask.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Kokumuo</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Archetype: Pilgrim</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Threshold: The Stricken</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Geist: Gahiji</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Keystone: Flute</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Kokumuo was a former slave, that was tossed out of the ship because he was sick. But he bounded with Gahiji, an african hunter that sweats blood. Kokumuo is very old and very thin, almost skeletal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>DEADMAN'S LOCKER</b></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">It is well known that in this time of the year there is a famous carnival celebration in Tortuga, where the local Sin-Eaters of the West Indies go to celebrate life, gather and trade information. The characters have recently died so their Geists inform them about the Carnival and how it's a good opportunity for them to find others like them and learn a bit more about their new condition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nicholas leaves from Port Royal hitch-hiking a merchant ship. During a small rain, the ship loses its course, but the Sin-Eater uses his navigation skills to bring it back on course, arriving in Tortuga just in time for the celebration. On port, he meets with Bernard, taking notice of his strange Geist, and they both make small conversation. Bernard spots some strange inscriptions on some rocks nearby and his Geist informs him that it is the Twilight Network, a collection of symbols that Sin-Eaters leave for each other to communicate. The message on the rocks gives a coordinate inside the island, so both Sin-Eaters decide to follow it, while they talk about how they hate the English. On the way to the coordinates, there is a tavern called the Horny Mermaid, and there is another Sin-Eater, Javier. The three of them talk about the festival, what they expect, how did they die and decide to get drunk while they wait for the festival to start. They hear rumors of a huge Man o' War that was seen around these waters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Meanwhile, Andrew managed to convince another crew of merchants to give him a ride to Tortuga as well in a small boat, because their pilot died of sickness and they were in need of one. However, while sneaking around he finds out the crew consists of english soldiers who wants to find information about Tortuga's defenses. So during the voyage Andrew poison them, one by one. Leaving only one that he kills with his blade when they arrive in Tortuga. The officers ghost argues with him (&quot;You've killed me!&quot;), but Andrew just ignores him till he finds his first Sin-Eater: Kokumuo. Kokumuo got there by exchanging favors with a portuguese sailor, talking with his dead brother and making both brothers making amends for things they did in life. They chat a little more, till they spot the Twilight Network symbols and decide to follow it. On the way, they spot a three-mast pirate ship with these same symbols in the flag, but decide to ignore it for now. They eventually get to the Horny Mermaid tavern and meet the other Sin-Eaters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The group interact a little, and find out they have a lot in common. They all hate the british empire, they're all short of cash, and they all can fill an essential position in a ship, and Andrew already got a ship. Kokumuo is the only one that doesn't fill a ship position, but his knowledge of death and ceremonies might be essential for a Sin-Eater krewe. Kokumuo also shares with the others that he is in Tortuga because of something his Geist told them: The Geist's previous Sin-Eater was on the trail of the treasure of a famous Sin-Eater named Bartholomew the Corpse-Eater. His final clue pointed him to Tortuga, but he died before getting there. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Krewe (though they're not a Krewe yet) decide to resume following the Twilight Network coordinates, and it takes them to a cave. Inside the cave a giant former slave named Adebowale meets them and lead them inside till they're with a blind Sea Hag named Amadi, with another former slave by her side, an old guy named Kwadwo. The Sea Hag is not a Sin-Eater, but a medium but she knows a lot of stuff about Sin-Eaters culture in the Caribbean. She says most Sin-Eaters around here are part of the Dreadful Krewe, lead by Captain Drowned Lilly. Drowned Lilly is a tyrant leader and those that doesn't join her krewe end up dead. The krewe consists of about seven sin-eaters, give or take. The Sea Hag hates Drowned Lilly, because she ate the ghost of her former lover. They talk about the possibility of joining her krewe, but end up deciding they wanna follow their own path, and ask if the Sea Hag knows something about the treasure of Bartholomew the Corpse-Eater. She is actually the lead that Gahiji's former Sin-Eater was trying to reach and she says she knows where they might find it because Drowned Lilly has been searching for it for a long time, and she doesn't want Lilly's krewe getting stronger.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Sea Hag tells them the treasure is hidden in a nearby small island, giving them coordinates and a scroll with ancient Twilight Network symbols that will help them. The group takes Andrew's two-mast ship and travel to the island indicated by the Sea Hag. They anchor the ship nearby and with a small boat get to the island's beach. The coordinates takes them through a forest, where a jaguar jumps Bernard, but Andrew takes it's head off. They follow through a large river and into a cave inside a waterfall. Inside it there's an avernian gate, which they open and enter, navigating through large passages with the help of twilight network symbols they can read thanks to the scroll the Sea Hag gave them. Nicholas uses his carthographing skills and it helps them a lot through it's passages, creating a map that doesn't let them lose their way. Kokumuo helps a thirsty and weak ghost to quench it's thirst, which helps him pass away, earning a lot of plasm for the krewe.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Eventually, they find a river with some strange pale white water and cross it, but Javier almost drowns. He feels a strange taste in the water, like it's messing with his head somewhat, but he didn't drink enough to have any full effect, so the group decides to fill a canteen with it. Then they finally cross the river, and more passages takes them to a dead dominion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">This dominion is like a giant cave, with water on the bottom and a stairway taking them to a slum city. The city is filled with skeletons and ghosts who drowned and it actually looks like a lively city, with ghosts playing dice, drinking in a tavern and there's even a brothel. They see a skeleton sitting at the entrance playing a lute and drinking rum, with a hat with coins to his side. Nicholas toss a coin in the hat and the skeleton tells them this Dominion is called Deadman' Locker. The rules are simple: Everything you take is yours, your word is your bound and if someone gives you something, you create a bond with that person. This last information causes a bit of a problem with Nicholas, who wants to take the coin back, and the Skeleton tells then that it might anger the Kerberoi of this dominion.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Not wanting any trouble with the Kerberoi, they leave the skeleton and try to find the Kerberoi so that they might find any information about Bartholomew the Corpse-Eater. The Kerberoi lives in a monastery and dresses like a monk. He has long horns, his teeth is like the husks of a boar and his eyes are rounded and bulged. He is Davy Jones, but they never get his name. Davy Jones tells them there was a Sin-Eater with this name around these parts, but he is long gone, and only his ship, The Corpse Whore, remains in the lower part of the dominion. The krewe takes the stairs to the waters, but there is a strange plasmic thing in the middle of the way. However, they can see a ship covered in seaweed that they feel a stronger death resonance then from the other ships below. The plasmic thing moves and looks threatening, so Kokumuo decides to jump to the water. But there are stalagmites below and he hurts himself badly and starts to drown. Andrew jumps and rescues Kokumuo, taking him to a little beach below and giving him mouth-to-mouth. Nicholas tries to climb down, but slips and hurts himself a little in the waters. Javier and Bernard jump around too, hurting themselves a little bit, but they all live.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Krewe swim to the Corpse Whore, and climb it, to be met with a skeleton crew with five ghosts. They're actually very weak and easily subjugated, so they end up agreeing to help the krewe. In the Captain's Cabin, there is a skeleton (a dead one, this time) with captains garb and a flintlock pistol to his side. The flintlock pistol is actually a deathmask that belonged to Bartholomew's Geist. Andrew takes the wheel and Nicholas spot a dark passage, while the rest of the crew take the sails. The dark passage leads throughout a shallow river, but Andrew manages to navigate it and eventually a little waterfall takes them out of the underworld and back to the way bellow the waterfall they've entered.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Back to the land of the living, they board the ship Andrew had stolen from the undercover privates and take all the provisions from it, heading back to Tortuga to talk to the Sea Hag. But Kokumuo thinks they need to increase their crew, so they go to a Cemetery and with the help of Nicholas' shovel he raises three zombis. Back to the ship, they spot an english merchant ship and decide to test The Corpse Whore. Andrew takes the ship nearby while Javier makes good use of the cannons to sink the merchant ship. The plan was to board it, but Javier probably shouldn't have used all those cannons. So they have to contend with taking whatever floats back, like some barrels of rum.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The crew wants to celebrate the new ship. They hire some whores, open a barrel of run and enjoy themselves. They all pass out, and have nightmares of Bartholomew the Corpse-Eater's time at the wheel. They see him growing paranoid while he gets old and talking with his Geist about hiding his treasure somewhere no one else but him might find out. He creates four maps in leather, giving them to his first-mates (second-mate, etc). But the maps only lead to their deaths. However, each map has a part of the true map, written with ink taken from his Geist so that only a Sin-Eater or a ghost might see it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The krewe wakes up, with a bit of a hung over and promises of riches in their eyes. Good times.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":196,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","user":"Max Deltree","date":". 12-31-2013, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/196-max-deltree","name":"Max Deltree","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar196_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank"